                                        "entry_id": "40bc0816-c3c7-3d34-93da-856eb8619fa4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A somewhat curved, single-edged medieval sword of European origin, with the cutting edge on its convex side, whose design is reminiscent of the Persian scimitar and the Chinese dao."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "attributive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91dcbf9a-1ece-4832-88e6-e093f36067cc",
                                                "sense_id": "3fae5a7b-fb44-3e9f-9e8c-521d1af50532",
                                                "text": "I haue seene the day, with my good biting Faulchion"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f7648b2-bd9b-4b95-8c47-69518069590c",
                                                "sense_id": "3fae5a7b-fb44-3e9f-9e8c-521d1af50532",
                                                "text": "Thy Chamber vvith Ambroſiall odors breatheth, / Nevv loues and true loues vnto them that entreateth, / And furious Mars made milde his Faulcheon ſheatheth / At thy delicious aſpect: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "332744c0-e4a4-4ac8-8021-13e8e49e733b",
                                                "sense_id": "3fae5a7b-fb44-3e9f-9e8c-521d1af50532",
                                                "text": "Even when the battle-roar was deep, / With dauntless heart he hewed his way, / Mid splintering lance and falchion-sweep, / And still was heard his warrior-lay; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c467ec2-e817-4006-bf36-a3aa8c62e84f",
                                                "sense_id": "3fae5a7b-fb44-3e9f-9e8c-521d1af50532",
                                                "text": "The Jester wore his usual fantastic habit, but late accidents had led him to adopt a good cutting falchion, instead of his wooden sword, with a targe to match it; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33c7b997-82c8-3cfa-8362-1db0cd0d3f00",
                                        "entry_id": "40bc0816-c3c7-3d34-93da-856eb8619fa4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A billhook."
                                        ],
